Project Overview

System: Real-time Driver Fatigue and Distraction Detection System.

Core Mechanism: Uses browser-based Edge Computing (MediaPipe) to analyze facial landmarks (eyes, mouth, head pose) and environment lighting.

Architecture & Tech Stack

Frontend: JavaScript (Modularized), HTML, CSS. Handles real-time video streaming, AI inference, logic calculation, and UI rendering.

Backend: Python (Flask). Acts as the central configuration and state management server.

Critical Development Rules (MUST FOLLOW)

Configuration-Driven (Strict):

NEVER hardcode logic thresholds, weights, or environment values (e.g., 220, 0.3, 1.5) in JavaScript files.

All configurations MUST be placed in the backend config.py and fetched via fetch("/api/config").

Coordinate Calculation Bug Prevention:

Because the UI uses transform: scaleX(-1) to mirror the video, NEVER use getBoundingClientRect() for Canvas or Video elements. Use clientWidth and clientHeight instead to prevent coordinate drifting.

MediaPipe Compatibility:

Do NOT set outputFaceBlendshapes: true in the FaceLandmarker initialization. It will crash the local .task model (FPS=0). Rely purely on 3D landmarks for pose detection.

Fatigue & Distraction Logic (Core Algorithms):

Dual-Track Scoring:

Chronic Fatigue: Calculate a 0-100 score based on PERCLOS (Percentage of Eye Closure over a time window), eye closure duration, and yawn rate. Apply penalty weights for nodding and looking away.

Critical Interception: Immediately force a 100% severe alert if microsleep (closure >= 1.5s), deep nodding (>= 1.5s), or a head snap occurs.

Head Snap (Nodding): Use a "0.3-second sliding window (Drop Delta)" for detection. Trigger if the current pitch drops significantly (e.g., > 0.06) from the maximum pitch within the last 0.3 seconds, rather than using frame-by-frame physical velocity.

Yawn Rate: Calculate based on the actual count of yawns within a strict 60-second sliding window, not the total runtime.

Distraction (Yaw): Determine looking away by calculating the horizontal distance ratio between the nose tip and the left/right cheeks.

